-- title:
--   Diamond automorphisms preserve the Gauss valuation subring
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and $M$ a nonzero natural number with $5 \le M$ and $p \nmid M$. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero which is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ of type $\{p\}$, and $\zeta \in L$ a primitive $p$-th root of unity. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $L \subseteq L((q))$ equal to [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.x1FunctionField (M * p))`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), that is, the $L$-subfield of $L((q))$ generated by the image, under the coefficientwise map $\mathbb{Q} \to L$ on Laurent series, of the $q$-expansion function field [`ModularCurve.x1FunctionFieldC ℚ`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L134) of $\Gamma_1(Mp)$ over $\mathbb{Q}$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$ such that $p$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$ and $\zeta$ lies in the image of $A \to L$, with an $A$-algebra structure on $K$ compatible with that on $L$. Let $j \in K$, nonzero, whose image in $L((q))$ is the coefficientwise image of [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157) $= q^{-1}\cdot\,$(the rational $j$-numerator power series). Let $d$ be coprime to $Mp$, and let $\theta$ be an $L$-algebra automorphism of $K$ which is compatible, through equality of images in $L((q))$, with the base change [`ModularCurve.baseChangeAut L (ModularCurve.diamondAut (M * p) d)`](def/ModularCurve_X1Diamond.html#L24) of the diamond automorphism $\langle d\rangle$ of [`ModularCurve.x1FunctionField (M * p)`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L137) — the latter being an automorphism $\sigma$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ satisfying [`ModularCurve.IsDiamondAut`](def/ModularCurve_X1Diamond.html#L53), i.e. acting on quotients of integral $q$-expansions of modular forms for $\Gamma_1(Mp)$ by the slash action of any $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(Mp)$ with $\gamma_{00} \equiv d \bmod Mp$ (and the identity if no such $\sigma$ exists). Finally let $W_0$ be a valuation subring of $K$ whose members are exactly those $f$ for which there exist $x, y \in A\llbracket q\rrbracket$ with the reduction of $y$ modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ nonzero and $f \cdot y(q) = x(q)$ in $L((q))$. Then for every $f \in K$ one has $\theta f \in W_0$ if and only if $f \in W_0$.
--
--   The subring $W_0$ is the Gauss valuation ring attached to the cusp $\infty$ of the level-$Mp$ modular function field over $L$, defined by $q$-expansions with coefficients in $A$ and nonvanishing reduction; the assertion is that it is stable under the diamond automorphism $\langle d\rangle$ for $d$ coprime to $Mp$. It is used in the study of the two-chart integral model of $X_1(Mp)$, where it yields that the minimal prime of the special fibre corresponding to $W_0$ is fixed by the diamond operators.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_XOneP_apply_mem_gaussValuationSubring_iff_of_apply_eq_diamondAut_x1_mul.lean

